  <prompt>Author the 2 GENUINELY GREENFIELD seeders replacing DeferredAppConfigSeeder's no-op placeholders for the field-mapping and chart-def scopes of H12bAppConfigSeedHandler.cs -- per DS-4 §2/§3: 'field-mapping + chart-def scopes = DeferredAppConfigSeeder no-op (C3.8 -- FR-16 half-delivered)... Half of FR-16 is undelivered -- second-strongest overstatement after H1/H13.' These have NEVER BEEN AUTHORED ANYWHERE in the repo (not even as a pwsh script to port) -- author them DIRECTLY as C# seeders using the SAME Dataverse Web API HttpClient idiom task 150/151 already established, per DS-1b's explicit framing: 'Must be authored from scratch anyway under every option; author directly as C# seeders, zero double-work.' Reference this project's Field Mapping Framework architecture doc for the field-mapping scope's data shape (sprk_fieldmapping records) and the chart-def scope's equivalent Dataverse table.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in authoring new Dataverse Web API seeders from a documented data-model reference (not a script to port), following an established in-process idiom.</role>

  <goal>Two new seeder classes exist: a field-mapping seeder writing the default/system sprk_fieldmapping seed rows (per docs/architecture/SPAARKE-FIELD-MAPPING-FRAMEWORK.md's schema), and a chart-def seeder writing the default chart-definition seed rows -- both via HttpClient + DefaultAzureCredential Dataverse Web API upserts, matching the idiom H12c/task 150/task 151 already prove. FR-16's full 4-scope delivery (DataGrid + workspace-layout + field-mapping + chart-def) is complete.</goal>

